PRIVATE REFLECTION: The question concerns a Steve McQueen watch slated for Sotheby’s New York 11 December 2024. Colleagues split on which lot is being referenced. Majority point to Steve McQueen’s personal Heuer Monaco Calibre 11 ref. 1133B, the blue-dial Le Mans watch, while a minority describe a Rolex Oyster Perpetual Submariner ref. 5513/5517. 

For the Heuer Monaco camp there is disagreement on dial layout and date position. Several colleagues place the date aperture at ~3 o’clock on the right side of the square dial and say the branding across the top is HEUER / MONACO / AUTOMATIC / CALIBRE 11, with SWISS MADE at 6 o’clock. Claims about what sits directly above the 3 o’clock window vary: 
- heuer as the brand logotype immediately above the aperture;
- monaco as the model name sitting immediately above/over the 3 o’clock date window;
- automatic as the line of the dial signature vertically immediately above the 3 o’clock window;
- swiss made as the marking immediately above the window, with some arguing the date is at 6 o’clock and Swiss Made sits above it;
- nothing / blank for a Submariner dial.

For the Rolex Submariner camp the date is at 3 o’clock with ROLEX / OYSTER PERPETUAL / SUBMARINER / 1000ft = 300m centered on the dial. Colleagues note the dial is blank immediately north of the aperture, so no dial printing sits directly above it, or they identify submariner / swiss made as the text in the vertical line above the aperture.

Unresolved points: which reference is actually in the 11 Dec 2024 Sotheby’s New York sale, whether the Monaco date is at 3 o’clock or 6 o’clock in the lot photography, and what printing is physically positioned directly north of the date window in the published catalog images. The most repeated specific text for the Heuer Monaco 1133B with a 3 o’clock date is monaco, with heuer and automatic also advanced, and swiss made advanced on the basis of a 6 o’clock date interpretation. The Rolex alternative is supported by some colleagues with nothing / submariner / swiss made as candidates. Need to verify the correct lot identity before locking the text above the date window.

